# fixture for sieve_rule/sieve_ruleset unit tests: a rule with two vars
# that share the REQUEST_ARGS collection type but differ in parse kind
# (ARGS -> values, ARGS_NAMES -> keys), used to check that sieving one
# doesn't leak onto the other. ARGS is listed first so a type-only match
# (the bug) would incorrectly pick vars[1] when sieving ARGS_NAMES.
SecRule ARGS|ARGS_NAMES "zzz_never_matches_zzz" "id:22222,phase:2,msg:'multi var sieve fixture',deny"
